# Lemely environment variables — copy to `.env` and fill in.
# `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# ── Gemini API key ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lemely talks to Google Gemini via the `google-genai` SDK. Any ONE of the
# variables below authenticates the CLI, the Gradio UI, AND the web portal.
# (Historically only LEMELY_GEMINI_API_KEY reached the web portal; the others
# left it silently degraded. That trap is fixed — all three now populate
# `settings.gemini_api_key`. Precedence: LEMELY_GEMINI_API_KEY > GEMINI_API_KEY
# > GOOGLE_API_KEY.)
#
# Pick one (LEMELY_GEMINI_API_KEY recommended for app-scoped clarity):
LEMELY_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=          # unprefixed; also read directly by the google-genai SDK
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=          # unprefixed SDK fallback

# ── Optional overrides (any Settings field via LEMELY_<SECTION>__<FIELD>) ─────
# LEMELY_GRADIO__PORT=7860
# LEMELY_LOGGING__LEVEL=INFO
# LEMELY_PATHS__OUTPUT_DIR=outputs

# ── Web backend bind (read directly by `python -m lemely.web`) ────────────────
# LEMELY_WEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# LEMELY_WEB_PORT=8000
